From 26893e1c73cae06ea67e75114fb4c9777ce4e285 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 00:47:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] patch 0232 -- opl3: honor patch[11] int8 transpose +
 8.3-safe bank filename

The DOPL3v1 runtime patch-bank loader (patch 0141) carried two latent
defects that only surface once a real bank is actually shipped:

1. 8.3 filename. The loader fopen'd "opl3-patches.dat" -- a 12-char base
   name that violates DOS 8.3. ResourceManager::getPath does no 8.3
   translation, so on the real MS-DOS target (g2k, no LFN driver) the
   engine asks for a name that cannot exist on an 8.3 FAT: the file is
   reported "not found" and the engine silently falls back to the 8-patch
   placeholder. Proven by DOSBox-X A/B (lfn=true loads 128; lfn=false
   not-found). Renamed to the 8.3-valid "opl3bank.dat" (fopen name + all
   log banners that print the filename).

2. patch[11] transpose never implemented. The DOPL3v1 record byte [11] is
   the engine-applied semitone transpose -- SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceWritePatch
   deliberately does `(void)patch[11]` ("engine applies before NoteOn"),
   but note_on ignored it. Real GM OPL banks (DMXOPL and every DMX/GENMIDI
   bank) voice instruments expecting playednote = midinote + offset; ~110
   of 128 programs carry -12. Without the transpose those play an octave
   too high (brighter/thinner). note_on now reads patch[11] as int8 and
   applies it to the value passed to the (fnum, block) calc only; the
   tracked midi_note is unchanged so note_off / _find_voice matching is
   unaffected.

Default-ON, no killswitch: the 8-patch placeholder constexprs all have
[11]=0, so with no opl3bank.dat present the transpose is 0 and behavior is
byte-identical to pre-0232.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
